The attached image illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan. Panel (A) displays a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, revealing spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface morphology, with a 50 nm scale bar. Panel (B) presents the size distribution determined by dynamic light scattering, showing that Nano-11 has a narrow size range with a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter of approximately 75-80 nm. This characterization is crucial as particle size and morphology influence cellular uptake by dendritic cells and the subsequent immune response, supporting its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.